these position vectors

06:11.261 --> 06:13.856
are going to keep specifying, we're gonna

06:13.856 --> 06:16.034
keep specifying points along this curve.

06:16.034 --> 06:19.364
So, the curve, let me draw the
curve in a different color.

06:19.364 --> 06:21.376
The curve looks something like this.

06:21.376 --> 06:22.537
It's meant to look exactly like

06:22.537 --> 06:24.325
the curve that I have up here.

06:24.325 --> 06:27.504
And, for example, r of b is going to be

06:27.504 --> 06:29.596
a vector that looks like this.

06:29.596 --> 06:33.125
It's going to be a vector
that looks like that.

06:33.125 --> 06:36.366
I want to draw it relatively straight.

06:36.366 --> 06:39.078
That vector, right there,

06:39.078 --> 06:42.508
is r of b.

06:42.508 --> 06:43.852
So, hopefully you realize that, look,

06:43.852 --> 06:46.174
